# API Conventions

## URL Structure (for Agent Briefs)

Agent briefs follow a structured format rather than URLs:

```
Spawn: Agent({name})
Brief:
  Context: {state summary}
  Inputs: {files to read}
  Task: {work to do}
  Constraints: {limitations}
```

## Response Format

Agents produce outputs to their default template paths. No explicit response format — output is file-based.

## Error Format

```
Gate Verification Report: {phase}

**Verdict:** {PASS / FAIL with N issues}

### Findings
| # | Criterion | Result | Evidence |
|---|-----------|--------|----------|
```

## Authentication

No authentication required. All operations within Claude Code session boundary.

## Pagination / Filtering / Sorting

Not applicable. File-based system with full reads.

## Rate Limiting

Not applicable. Single-agent execution per phase.
